; Regression: a parenless call whose ARGUMENT is itself a call is dropped whole,
; and was silent until the effect-free-statement gate named it (2026-08-15).
;
; `scaly_eputs s.to_c_string()` emits NEITHER call — not the extern, not
; `to_c_string`. Measured against the pre-change compiler: two `scaly_eputs`
; statements in the source, ONE `call void @_Z11scaly_eputs...` in the IR, and no
; `to_c_string` anywhere. The one that survives is the one whose argument is a
; plain literal.
;
; This shape was described as "silently drops or mis-parses" and that was
; half right: through a MEMBER receiver (`vec.add helper(2)`) the arity gate
; catches it and says `got 0, expected 1`. Through a FREE function there is no
; arity to check against, so the collapse leaves an unnamed operator call behind
; and the statement evaporates.
;
; It was live in the tree: dazzle_cli.scaly's JIT-selftest failure branch built
; a "FAILED at step N" message and printed only the newline after it.
;
; xfail: this statement did not resolve to a call

package scaly 0.1.0

function probe() returns int
{
    var sb StringBuilder()
    sb.append "hi"
    let s sb.to_string()
    scaly_eputs s.to_c_string()
    1
}

let r probe()
print "unreachable"
